answer:
The minimum age for remote pilots operating a UAS in the open category shall be 16 years [reg-2019-947 | Article 9 - Minimum age for remote pilots].

No minimum age is required when:
* Operating in subcategory A1 with a UAS Class C0 that is a toy within the meaning of Directive 2009/48/EC [reg-2019-947 | Article 9 - Minimum age for remote pilots];
* Operating privately-built UAS with a maximum take-off mass of less than 250g [reg-2019-947 | Article 9 - Minimum age for remote pilots];
* Operating under the direct supervision of a remote pilot complying with Article 9(1) and Article 8 [reg-2019-947 | Article 9 - Minimum age for remote pilots].

Member States may lower the minimum age for remote pilots operating in the open category by up to 4 years [reg-2019-947 | Article 9 - Minimum age for remote pilots]. Where a Member State lowers the minimum age, those remote pilots shall only be allowed to operate a UAS on the territory of that Member State [reg-2019-947 | Article 9 - Minimum age for remote pilots]. Additionally, Member States may define UAS geographical zones pursuant to Article 15 [reg-2019-947 | Article 15 - Operational conditions for UAS geographical zones].

